// v0.1 - NEW instance DB for SFB4 (IEC TON, on-delay timer), replacing
//   classical timer T50 (underfill settle, 5s). Switched from classical
//   S5 timers to SFB4 per Michou's request ("Timers don't start!!! What
//   about using SFB4 instead?") - see FC155 v0.26 changelog for the
//   full reasoning (the real bug: "SD" is the NON-retentive on-delay
//   mnemonic, not the stored one as this project's comments wrongly
//   claimed all session; separately, SFB4 itself is call-driven, not
//   hardware-autonomous like classical timers, so it must be CALLed
//   every scan for its whole duration, not just once).
//   DB number (106) is a best guess, free within this repo's own
//   tracked files - not independently confirmed against the live
//   project's full block list, same caution already flagged for
//   T52-T56 and never fully closed out.
